  message: "Satisfied. Merged as PR #1853 (dev cd93704544). Kotlin's _kt_receiver_module and scala's typed-receiver call arm now fall through to static_owner_module -- the closed java.lang list and shadow exclusions the static-call arm uses -- for a bare declared type the file never imports. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE on merged dev: (1) this item's own filed probe, re-run through analyze_kotlin / analyze_scala: kotlin u(p: Process) p.getInputStream() -> kotlin:java.lang.Process:0-0:getInputStream (was external); kotlin v p.inputStream -> kotlin:java.lang.Process:0-0:getInputStream (was NO edge); kotlin w (qualified control) unchanged; scala s p.getInputStream() -> scala:java.lang.Process (was external); scala t parameterless unchanged -- all five arms now agree, which is the statement. (2) The consequence measured in the 2026-10-25 premise check: `hypergumbo verify-claims` with \"No subprocess launches\" on `fun f(pb: ProcessBuilder) { pb.start() }` (kotlin) and the scala equivalent now exits 1 with the claim VIOLATED; before the fix it exited 3, confirmed_with_caveats. (3) test_jvm_declared_java_lang_receiver.py (14 tests, 8 red before): bare ProcessBuilder / Runtime classify as subprocess; a project ProcessBuilder, an imported org.other.ProcessBuilder and a shadowed kotlin String / scala Iterable keep their own answer. NOT measured: the corpus count of typed receivers this reaches."  # 227b
